<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Quick Settings tile icon.

  Deliberately NOT the adaptive launcher foreground: that asset reserves the outer third of its canvas
  as the adaptive-icon safe zone, so its artwork covers only the inner ~66% and the tile rendered
  visibly smaller than every other app's. Here the ring runs right to the viewport edge, which is the
  largest the system will draw it.

  Quick Settings tints tile icons by ALPHA and ignores their colour, so everything is opaque white and
  the shape alone carries the image. No background disc, or the tile would tint into a solid blob.

  Geometry follows the source logo (878x878, mask-composited). Reconstructed without <mask>, which
  VectorDrawable has no equivalent for:
   - the source ring is a r=605.5 circle stroked 440 wide (so it spans r 385.5..825.5) intersected with
     the r=439 artboard disc, i.e. an annulus 385.5..439. Drawn directly as a r=412.25 circle stroked
     53.5 wide, which is the same band without needing a clip — and antialiases cleanly, which a
     clipped stroke would not.
   - the bottom-left quadrant still needs clipping (it runs to x=-42, y=919 in the source). Its clip
     radius is pulled in to 410 so the cut lands UNDER the ring and the seam is never visible.
   - the crow path needs no clip at all: it peaks at r~354, well inside the ring.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="878"
    android:viewportHeight="878">

    <group>
        <clip-path android:pathData="M439,29 a410,410 0 1,0 0,820 a410,410 0 1,0 0,-820 Z" />
        <path
